  "pr_observation": {
    "url": "https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave/pull/20",
    "number": 20,
    "state": "closed",
    "merged": true,
    "mergeable": false,
    "draft": false,
    "body": "## Why\nNativeWeave now has one product: strongly typed C# Fluent ORM for PostgreSQL and SQLite, backed by Rust SeaQuery/SQLx with Native AOT and precompiled NuGet assets. Perf-01 is terminated; old NativeWeave#19 and Plan#23 were closed unmerged. Plan#24 established the new scope before Design#14 and implementation edits.\n\n## Changes\n- Preserve Database Host, providers, sources/pools/sessions, transactions, migrations, parameters, Fluent/static model/DTO mapping, relations/CRUD, streams, cancellation, errors, disposal and C#\u2013Rust bindings.\n- Remove owned HTTP/gRPC servers, routing/protocol wrappers, MCP, server examples, independent compression/proof/demo engines, HelloWorld, orphan generic generators/analyzers, benchmarks and scaffold products.\n- Preserve unique database coverage from mixed reference/end-to-end services as finite direct C# business fixtures, including keyset/cursor isolation, conflict/COMMIT-loss recovery, transaction/session/stream retirement and filesystem/outbox recovery.\n- Reconcile Cargo/.NET/default builds, native assets, twelve database candidate packages, packaging, CI, examples and documentation. Retire HelloWorld public auto-publication. Application developers choose their own standard HTTP/gRPC host; this PR adds no hosting wrapper or ORM feature.\n- Keep strict formatting, API/XML/DocFX, locked dependencies, negative guards, security, provenance and source-drift checks. Necessary test/fixture repairs preserve all existing rejection cases; database runtime/API/ABI implementation and external dependency versions are unchanged.\n\n## Exact final validation\nCandidate `7255040b9501a1898d008c793f9b1777d8394d65`, tree `5f5d74ec7cfa502a4f8d119bb89e2e2776d4b65b`, passed [complete CI44919645468](https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave/actions/runs/44919645468): all six jobs and every mandatory build step succeeded.\n\n- Rust workspace: 86 tests passed, none failed or ignored; complete locked .NET build, formatting and exact API/XML/DocFX checks executed.\n- All 56 ordered database regression gates passed against real PostgreSQL18 and SQLite, including full Host, migrations, materialization, Fluent and relations JIT/AOT suites.\n- Outside-source ordinary PackageReference consumers passed all PostgreSQL/SQLite JIT/AOT cells and all three SQLite/PostgreSQL/combined graphs with typed Fluent queries, DTO values and ordinary source edits.\n- Exact package, output and mapped-native identities agree. Twelve candidates contain only the two expected provider native leaves and retained database dependencies.\n- Genuine pinned SDK consumption without Rust, four runtime-only transfers without SDK/compilers, four lifecycle/business rows, 32 finite faults, 14 release/recovery cases and 24 refusal guards in each full consumer environment passed.\n- Unchanged semantic validator/v3 contract passed 2,959 predicates across 17 sections. Independent regression review checked all 56 outer logs and 668 immutable-source hashes across 426 paths.\n- Both downloaded artifacts matched GitHub SHA256/size; independent reviewers rehashed both ZIPs and all 1,046 extracted files.\n\n[Committed Plan acceptance evidence](https://github.com/IzuSharp/Plan/blob/07f8ded8f05ebbb0770d54634246b57ba7b2f5c3/ledger/evidence/batches/DB-Scope-01/results/linux-acceptance-summary.md) contains the actual results, original safe JSON exports, source review chain, artifact inventories and reviewer limitations. The generic successful formatter workspace-load warning and Cargo manifest warning remain disclosed. Historical failed/cancelled/development/local attempts retain their original identities, including the local tmpfs-full attempt; none is relabeled as this final CI.\n\nIndependent reviews are agent technical reviews, not second-account GitHub approvals. Design#14 is merged at `8298dc4128b745cf1809bad0c3cf02c45eb7f522` with both exact main checks successful. Product merge/main CI and the remaining Plan closeout are tracked separately in Plan#24.\n\nNo performance optimization, 30-minute load, public NuGet publication, license/protection change or unrelated Dependabot PR3/4/7 change is included.",
